COAM Update mcs via webUI
    [Timeout]  5 min
    [Documentation]    Author: Ding Binmei HGZ_SG4
    ...                Description: Update MCS value for UL or DL from webui
    ...                ${direct}: value can be ul or dl, case is not sensitive
    ...                ${cell}: value can be NRCELL-1, NRCELL-2..., defult to use NRCELL-1
    [Arguments]    ${direct}    ${mcs_value}    ${cell}=NRCELL-1    ${download_dir}=${TS_CASE_LOG_PATH}
    ...    ${url}=https://${tl.gnbs[0].cu.oam_http_connection_details.addr}
    ...    ${username}=${tl.gnbs[0].cu.oam_http_connection_details.username}    ${password}=${tl.gnbs[0].cu.oam_http_connection_details.password}
    ${mcs_value}    Convert to string    ${mcs_value}
    ${direct}    Convert to uppercase    ${direct}
    ${par_name}    set variable if    "${direct}"=="UL"    Initial MCS for UL Transmission    Initial MCS for DL transmission
    COAM Navigate to login page via webUI    download_dir=${download_dir}
    ${mcs_pre}    selenium_coam.get_parameter_value    dist_name=${cell}    filter_param=${par_name}
    Run keyword if    ${mcs_pre}==${mcs_value}
    ...    Log to console    Current MCS value is ${mcs_pre}, no need to update
    ...    ELSE    Run keywords
    ...                selenium_coam.set_parameter_value    dist_name=${cell}    filter_param=${par_name}     new_value=${mcs_value}    AND
    ...                Log to console    Update ${direct} MCS value from ${mcs_pre} to ${mcs_value} for ${cell}    AND
    ...                selenium_coam.validate_plan    AND
    ...                selenium_coam.activate_plan    activate_plan_despite_errors=${True}    AND
    ...                COAM Verify if mcs is updated successfully via webUI    par_name=${par_name}    expect_mcs_value=${mcs_value}
    [Teardown]    COAM selenium logout

COAM Verify if mcs is updated successfully via webUI
    [Documentation]    Author: Ding Binmei HGZ_SG4    [PRIVATE]
    ...                Description: Verify if MCS value is updated successfully from webui
    ...                ${par_name}: Value can be: should be the paramer name
    ...                ${cell}: value can be NRCELL-1, NRCELL-2..., defult to use NRCELL-1
    [Arguments]    ${par_name}    ${expect_mcs_value}    ${cell}=NRCELL-1
    ${mcs_actual}    selenium_coam.get_parameter_value    dist_name=${cell}    filter_param=${par_name}
    Should be equal as strings    ${mcs_actual}    ${expect_mcs_value}    msg=MCS value is not updated successfully for ${par_name} of ${cell}

COAM Verify NIDD parameter error via webUI
    [Documentation]  Author: Ding Binmei
    ...              Description: Input with invalid value and do validation for the pop up message
    ...              ${exp_error_message}: Refers to the error message pops up from web UI
    ...              ${value}: Refers to the invalid value for NIDD
    ...              Please noticed that all the bellow filter criterias are case sensitive, values should be matched from webUI,
    ...              otherwise filter validation will failed
    ...              ${object_name}: Refers to the filter field for 'Object name' from web UI
    ...              ${parameter_name}: Refers to the filter field for 'Parameter name' from web UI
    ...              ${abbr_name}: Refers to the filter field for 'Abbreviation' from web UI
    [Arguments]    ${exp_error_message}    ${value}    ${object_name}    ${parameter_name}    ${abbr_name}=${EMPTY}
    ...            ${download_dir}=${TS_CASE_LOG_PATH}
    COAM Navigate to login page via webUI    download_dir=${download_dir}
    selenium_coam.set_parameter_value    dist_name=${object_name}    abbr=${abbr_name}    filter_param=${parameter_name}     new_value=${value}
    ${validate_message}    selenium_coam.get_error_info_after_set_parameter
    Should be equal as strings    ${validate_message}    ${exp_error_message}
    ...             msg=Validate error message for NIDD parameter ${abbr_name} failed, expected error message ${exp_error_message} is not found.
    [Teardown]    COAM selenium logout

COAM Verify pmax validate message
    [Documentation]    Author: Ding Binmei
