COAM Save snapshot via webUI
    [Documentation]  Author: Ding Binmei
    ...              Description: Snapshot logs will be stored under the indicate download_dir
    [Arguments]    ${download_dir}=${TS_CASE_LOG_PATH}    ${url}=https://${tl.gnbs[0].cu.oam_http_connection_details.addr}
    ...    ${username}=${tl.gnbs[0].cu.oam_http_connection_details.username}    ${password}=${tl.gnbs[0].cu.oam_http_connection_details.password}
    ${temp_dir_for_save_snapshot}    Set variable    /tmp/snapshot_ta
    Create directory    ${temp_dir_for_save_snapshot}
    COAM Navigate to login page via webUI    download_dir=${temp_dir_for_save_snapshot}    url=${url}    username=${username}    password=${password}
    ${is_startup_window_exist}=      selenium_coam.start_up_view_window_exists
    Run Keyword If    ${is_startup_window_exist}    Run Keyword And Ignore Error    selenium_coam.close_start_up_view_window
    selenium_coam.snapshot_collection_settings    coverage=All log files    save_location=Local
    ${temp_snapshot_file_path}    selenium_coam.collect_snapshot
    Wait until keyword succeeds    2min    2sec    File should not be empty    ${temp_snapshot_file_path}
    ${final_snapshot_file_path}    Wait until keyword succeeds    3x    200ms    Copy file and verify file exists
    ...    source_file_path=${temp_snapshot_file_path}    dest_file_folder=${download_dir}
    [Return]    ${final_snapshot_file_path}
    [Teardown]    Run keywords    COAM selenium logout    AND
    ...    Run keyword and ignore error    Empty directory    path=${temp_dir_for_save_snapshot}

COAM is unit contained in updated parameter
    [Documentation]  Author: Ding Binmei  [PRIVATE]
    ...              Description: Check if unit is included in the updated parameter
    ...              check if there is unit key in ${dict_update_parameter_info_via_webui}
    [Arguments]    ${dict_update_parameter_info_via_webui}
    ${is_unit_contained}    Run keyword and return status  dictionary should contain key
    ...           dictionary=${dict_update_parameter_info_via_webui}    key=unit
    [Return]    ${is_unit_contained}

COAM Verify if all parameters successfully updated via webUI
    [Documentation]  Author: Ren Biyao  [PRIVATE]
    ...              Description: this keyword is to check if all the parameters updated successfully.
    ...              2019-9-12 Ding Binmei: Added logic to cover scenario for parameter with unit included like ms, dB
    ...    ${parameters_to_update_via_webui} should be given in special format, just as the following:
    ...    ${parameters_to_update_via_webui}=[{'abbr': 'qciTab5Nsa3x', 'dist_name': 'NRBTS-1', 'filter_param': 'UL data path',
    ...    'new_value': 'ulOverLteNr'}, , {'filter_param': 'Radio link resume back-off timer', 'new_value': '6005', 'dist_name': 'NRBTS-243',
    ...    'abbr': 'rlResumeBackOffTmr', 'unit': 'ms'}]
    ...    abbr: refers to the 'Abbreviation' field from webui. Its value can be None or exact value as the 'Abbreviation' field of webui.
    ...    dist_name: can be 'NRBTS-1', 'NRCELL-1'
    ...    filter_parameter: is full Parameter name, which should be the same as the BTS shows.
    ...    unit: Only required if some parameters have unit, otherwise verification will be failed
    [Arguments]    ${parameters_to_update_via_webui}
    FOR  ${cur_para_to_update}  IN  @{parameters_to_update_via_webui}
      ${actual_para_value}    selenium_coam.get_parameter_value
      ...    dist_name=${cur_para_to_update['dist_name']}
      ...    abbr=${cur_para_to_update['abbr']}
      ...    filter_param=${cur_para_to_update['filter_param']}
      ${is_unit_contained_in_parameter}    COAM is unit contained in updated parameter
      ...                                           dict_update_parameter_info_via_webui=${cur_para_to_update}
      Run keyword if    ${is_unit_contained_in_parameter}
      ...    should be equal as strings    '${actual_para_value}'    '${cur_para_to_update['new_value']}${cur_para_to_update['unit']}'
      ...                                   msg=current parameter to update is ${cur_para_to_update}, and value update fail
      ...    ELSE    Should be equal as strings    '${actual_para_value}'    '${cur_para_to_update['new_value']}'
      ...                                   msg=current parameter to update is ${cur_para_to_update}, and value update fail
    END

COAM Update several parameters via webUI
    [Documentation]  Author: Ren Biyao
    ...              Description: this keyword is to update several parameters via COAM webUI.
    ...              2019-9-12 Ding Binmei: Added logic to cover scenario for parameters with unit included like ms, dB...
    ...              2019-11-21 Jia Lei: Add check gnb on air for parameters which will cause gnb restart after activate.
    ...    ${parameters_to_update_via_webui} should be given in special format, just as the following:
    ...    ${parameters_to_update_via_webui}=[{'abbr': 'qciTab5Nsa3x', 'dist_name': 'NRBTS-1', 'filter_param': 'UL data path',
    ...    'new_value': 'ulOverLteNr'}, {'filter_param': 'Radio link resume back-off timer', 'new_value': '6005', 'dist_name': 'NRBTS-243',
    ...    'abbr': 'rlResumeBackOffTmr', 'unit': 'ms'}]
    ...    abbr: refers to the 'Abbreviation' field from webui. Its value can be None or exact value as the 'Abbreviation' field of webui.
    ...    dist_name: refers to the 'object name' field from webui. Its value can be 'NRBTS-1', 'NRCELL-1'
    ...    filter_parameter: refers to 'Parameter name' field from webui. Its value should be the same as the BTS shows.
    ...    unit: Only required if some parameters have unit, otherwise verification will be failed
    ...    ${diff_para} is used as a flag to check if we have any parameter to update. If the length of this variable remains [],
    ...    which means that all the parameters are the same as what we already have, then no need for validation and activation.
    ...    ${is_need_to_check_validation_errors} is a flag to decide whether validation errors will check or not.
    ...    If set to ${False}, then no validation errors will check; if set to ${True}, then validation error will check.
    ...    ${is_gnb_restrat_after_online_modify} is a flag to check whether gnb will be restarted after activate paln.
    ...    default is set to ${False}, then no gnb restart; if set to ${True}, then gnb will be restarted after activate plan..
    [Arguments]      ${parameters_to_update_via_webui}    ${download_dir}
    ...       ${is_need_to_check_validation_errors}=${False}
    ...       ${is_gnb_restrat_after_online_modify}=${False}
    COAM Navigate to login page via webUI    download_dir=${download_dir}
    @{diff_para} =    create list
    FOR  ${cur_para_to_update}  IN  @{parameters_to_update_via_webui}
      ${cur_para_value}    selenium_coam.get_parameter_value
      ...    dist_name=${cur_para_to_update['dist_name']}
      ...    abbr=${cur_para_to_update['abbr']}
      ...    filter_param=${cur_para_to_update['filter_param']}
      Run keyword if    '${cur_para_value}'=='${cur_para_to_update['new_value']}'
      ...    Log to console    current value is ${cur_para_value}, no need to update
      ...    ELSE    run keywords
      ...    selenium_coam.set_parameter_value
      ...    dist_name=${cur_para_to_update['dist_name']}
      ...    abbr=${cur_para_to_update['abbr']}
      ...    filter_param=${cur_para_to_update['filter_param']}
      ...    new_value=${cur_para_to_update['new_value']}    AND
      ...    Append to list    ${diff_para}    ${cur_para_to_update}
    END
    Run keyword if    ${diff_para}    run keywords
    ...    selenium_coam.validate_plan    AND
    ...    COAM check validation errors from webui
    ...    is_need_to_check_validation_errors=${is_need_to_check_validation_errors}    AND
    ...    selenium_coam.activate_plan    activate_plan_despite_errors=${True}    AND
    ...    COAM Verify gnb on air after activate plan via webUI
    ...    is_gnb_restrat_after_online_modify=${is_gnb_restrat_after_online_modify}    AND
    ...    COAM Verify if all parameters successfully updated via webUI
    ...    parameters_to_update_via_webui=${diff_para}
    ...    ELSE
    ...    Log to console    All parameters are the same as what already set on webui, and no need to update!
    [Teardown]    COAM selenium logout

COAM check validation errors from webui
    [Documentation]    This keyword is to set the flag to decide whether need to get validation errors or not.
    ...    If ${is_need_to_check_validation_errors} set to True, the get validation errors will require.
    ...    If ${is_need_to_check_validation_errors} set to False, the get validation errors will not carry out.
    [Arguments]     ${is_need_to_check_validation_errors}
    Run keyword if    ${is_need_to_check_validation_errors}==${True}
    ...    COAM verify validation errors are empty from webui
    ...    ELSE    Log to console    No need to get validation errors!

COAM verify validation errors are empty from webui
    [Documentation]  Author: Ren Biyao  [PRIVATE]
    ...              Description: This keyword is to get three kinds of errors from webui, which come from definition errors tag,
    ...              hardware errors tag, and relation errors tag from webui.
    @{errors} =    create list
    ${defination_errors}    selenium_coam.get_definition_errors
    ${relation_errors}      selenium_coam.get_relation_errors
    ${hardware_errors}      selenium_coam.get_hardware_errors
    ${errors}    combine lists    ${defination_errors}   ${relation_errors}    ${hardware_errors}
    Log to console    The current BTS exist errors as ${errors}.
    Should be empty    ${errors}

COAM Check GNB cell on air via WebUI
    [Documentation]  Author: Jia Lei
    ...              Description: Check if GNB is in cell on air status via webui
    [Arguments]    ${download_dir}=${TS_CASE_LOG_PATH}
    COAM Navigate to login page via webUI    download_dir=${download_dir}
    ${is_startup_window_exist}=      selenium_coam.start_up_view_window_exists
    Run Keyword If    ${is_startup_window_exist}    Run Keyword And Ignore Error    selenium_coam.close_start_up_view_window
    ${bts_status}    selenium_coam.get_bts_status
    Should be equal as strings    ${bts_status}    On air    msg=GNB is not on air, Current status is ${bts_status}
    ...                      ignore_case=${True}
    [Teardown]    COAM selenium logout

COAM Verify gnb on air after activate plan via webUI
    [Documentation]  Author: Jia Lei
    ...    Description: GNB will be restarted after online modifiction.
    ...                Check gnb is on air after restart.
    ...    If ${is_gnb_restrat_after_online_modify} set to True, gnb will be restarted after activate plans.
    ...    If ${is_gnb_restrat_after_online_modify} set to False, gnb will not be restarted after activate plans.
    [Arguments]     ${is_gnb_restrat_after_online_modify}=${False}    ${download_dir}=${TS_CASE_LOG_PATH}
    Run keyword if    ${is_gnb_restrat_after_online_modify}== ${True}    run keywords
    ...    sleep    60s    reason=Wait for gnb Restart    AND
    ...    COAM selenium logout    AND
    ...    wait until keyword succeeds    15 min    20 sec    COAM Check GNB cell on air via WebUI    AND
    ...    COAM Navigate to login page via webUI    download_dir=${download_dir}
    ...    ELSE    Log to console    No need to restart gnb after activate plan!

